[Character data and commands to conduct the phylogenetic analyses presented in:
Cole, Wright, and Hopkins, Phylogenetic position and stratigraphic uncertainty of a new flexible crinoid 
from the Ordovician-Silurian boundary of Anticosti Island (Quebec, Canada): Journal of Paleontology.]

[Characters and character states associated with the matrices below:
1. Calyx shape ratio (height/width) measured at the top of the radials: 0: very high: > 1.0; 1: intermediate 1.0-0.5; 2: low: < 0.5
2.  Calyx/aboral cup profile to the top of the radials: 0: cone shaped (~straight sides); 1: bowl shaped (rounded base, vertical sides); 2: globe/barrel shaped (rounded base, widest below the summit of cup)
3.  Number of infrabasal plates: 0: five 1: three; 2: one
4.  Infrabasal plate dimensions: 0: W>H; 1: H~W; 2: H>W
5.  Basal plate dimensions: 0: W>H; 1: H~W; 2: H>W
6.  Basal plates, relative sizes (including CD basal): 0: subequal; 1: unequal
7.  Radial plate largest plate in calyx: 0: no; 1: yes
8.  Number of posterior plates partially or completely in cup at or below height of radials: 0: > three; 1: ≤ three
9.  Radianal plate shape: 0: pentagonal; 1: tetragonal; 2: hexagonal/septagonal
10. Proximal position of radianal plate: 0: full width beneath C radial plate; 1: to left and below C radial plate; 2: within radial circlet above the CD basal
11. Anal X presence: 0: absent; 1: present
12. Anal X shape: 0: pentagonal; 1: hexagonal; 2: 7 or more sides
13. Right tube plate presence: 0: absent; 1: present
14. Presence of an anal sac: 0: absent; 1: present
15. Height of the anal opening above the aboral cup: 0:  0 - 0.5x height of the arms; 1: 0.5 - 1.0x height of arms; 2: > height of the arms
16. Anus position relative to crown: 0: near the summit; 1: below the summit
17. Dominant medial column supporting sac: 0: absent; 1: present 
18. Tube-like anal series: 0: absent; 1: present
19. Lower brachials fixed: 0: absent; 1: present
20. Fixed rays (i.e., interlocking): 0: absent; 1: present
21. Interradial plates ("interbrachials" of some): 0: absent; 1: present
22. Patelloid process: 0: absent; 1: present
23. Highest position of axillary on primibrachials located in B-E rays: 0: IPr1; 1: IPr2; 2: ≥ IPr3
24. Spacing between insertion of axillaries on main axis at and above the second brachitaxes in B-E rays: 0: regular; 1: irregular
25. Overall outline pattern of arm bifurcations [see Ubaghs, 1978; fig. 115]: 0: isotomous; 1:  heterotomous [= 2 and 3 in Fig. 115 of Treatise]; 2: endotomous; 3: exotomous
]


[
****************************************
PHYLOGENETIC ANALYSES AND CHARACTER LIST
****************************************

Character data and commands to run three phylogenetic analyses are provided below:

(1): Maximum parsimony
(2): Bayesian inference (topology only)
(3): Bayesian fossil tip-dating (divergence time estimation)

To repeat an analysis, be sure that the correct matrix and commands have their brackets (i.e., []'s) removed, 
then just execute the .nex file in the appropriate program (PAUP* or MrBayes).
]

[
#NEXUS

BEGIN TAXA;
	DIMENSIONS NTAX=12;
	TAXLABELS
		Cupulocrinus Homalocrinus Icthyocrinus Protaxocrinus Hormocrinus Ladacrinus Proanisocrinus Tintinnabulicrinus Paerticrinus Kyphosocrinus Anticosticrinus Anisocrinus 
	;

END;


BEGIN CHARACTERS;
	DIMENSIONS  NCHAR=25; 
	FORMAT DATATYPE = STANDARD GAP = - MISSING = ? SYMBOLS = "  0 1 2 3 4 5";
	MATRIX
	Cupulocrinus        10011 10100 11011 01100 11200 
	Homalocrinus        20100 11122 0?0?0 00010 11112
	Icthyocrinus        20101 0?100 0?000 10011 01110
	Protaxocrinus       10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100
	Hormocrinus         21100 11102 ???0? ?0010 11100
	Ladacrinus          10101 11111 1011? ?0110 10110
	Proanisocrinus      20101 11100 1010? ?0010 10100
	Tintinnabulicrinus  21??2 11122 0?0?? ?0010 11112
	Paerticrinus        21??1 11100 1211? ?0110 10210
	Kyphosocrinus	    11101 01100 120?? ?0010 10112
	Anticosticrinus	    10100 01100 120?? ?0010 10110
	Anisocrinus	    101?0 01100 1100? ?0010 10110
;

END;
]
[
**********************************
MAXIMUM PARSIMONY ANALYSIS IN PAUP
**********************************

*Runs a 'branch and bound' maximum parsimony analysis.
Excludes parsimony-uniformative characters.
All character changes are unordered and equally weighted.

]

BEGIN PAUP;
Outgroup 1;
Exclude Uninf;
BandB;
Contree;

END;

[
****************************************************
UNDATED BAYESIAN ANALYSIS IN MRBAYES (TOPOLOGY ONLY)
****************************************************

*Runs a Bayesian analysis of phylogeny using only character data and basic Mk model [sampling all variable characters].
Returns 50% majority rule consensus tree.

]
[
BEGIN MRBAYES;
set autoclose = yes nowarn = yes;
lset rates = equal coding = variable;
prset Brlenspr = Unconstrained : GammaDir ( 1.0 , 0.100 , 1.0 , 1.0 );
mcmcp ngen = 100000 samplefreq = 50 printfreq = 100 nruns = 2 nchains = 4 relburnin = yes burninfrac = 0.25 temp = 0.1 savebrlens = yes;
mcmc;
sump;
sumt;

END;

]

[
**********************************************
BAYESIAN FOSSIL TIP-DATING ANALYSIS IN MRBAYES
**********************************************

*Runs a Bayesian fossil tip-dating analysis using both character and stratigraphic data to estimate divergence times.
Uses results from undated analyses to constrain tree topology.
The sampled ancestor implementation of the fossilized birth-death process (SA-FBD) == prior on trees and branch lengths.
Samples additional species and genera (currently lacking character data) to improve parameter estimation.
Independent gamma rates model used to 'relax' the morphological clock.
All SA-FBD and morphological clock priors intentionally set to be flat and/or vague. 

]



#NEXUS

BEGIN DATA;
	DIMENSIONS  NTAX=42 NCHAR=25;
	FORMAT DATATYPE=standard SYMBOLS="012345" MISSING=?;

MATRIX
Cupulocrinus_humilis       		10011 10100 11011 01100 11200
Cupulocrinus_angustatus    		10011 10100 11011 01100 11200
Cupulocrinus_canaliculatus 		10011 10100 11011 01100 11200
Cupulocrinus_crossmani			10011 10100 11011 01100 11200
Cupulocrinus_heterocostalis		10011 10100 11011 01100 11200
Cupulocrinus_jewetti			10011 10100 11011 01100 11200
Cupulocrinus_levorsoni			10011 10100 11011 01100 11200
Cupulocrinus_polydactylus		10011 10100 11011 01100 11200
Cupulocrinus_sepulchrum			10011 10100 11011 01100 11200
Proanisocrinus_oswegoensis		20101 11100 1010? ?0010 10100
Anisocrinus_prinstaensi			101?0 01100 1100? ?0010 10110
Anisocrinus_interradiatus		101?0 01100 1100? ?0010 10110
Protaxocrinus_ovalis			10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100
Protaxocrinus_aberrans			10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100
Protaxocrinus_amii				10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100
Protaxocrinus_anellus			10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100
Protaxocrinus_cataractensis		10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100
Protaxocrinus_elegans			10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100
Protaxocrinus_girardeau		 	10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100
Protaxocrinus_girvanensis		10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100
Protaxocrinus_interbrachiatus	10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100
Protaxocrinus_laevis		   	10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100
Protaxocrinus_paraios			10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100
Protaxocrinus_robustus			10101 1?100 1001? ?1110 11100    
Tintinnabulicrinus_estoniensis	21??2 11122 0?0?? ?0010 11112
Paerticrinus_arvosus			21??1 11100 1211? ?0110 10210
Ladacrinus_asynaptos			10101 11111 1011? ?0110 10110
Icthyocrinus_laevus				20101 0?100 0?000 10011 01110
Icthyocrinus_gotlandicus		20101 0?100 0?000 10011 01110
Clidochirus_anebos				????? ????? ????? ????? ?????
Clidochirus_americanus			????? ????? ????? ????? ?????
Clidochirus_serrulatus			????? ????? ????? ????? ?????
Clidochirus_vaurealensis		????? ????? ????? ????? ?????
Clidochirus_springeri			????? ????? ????? ????? ?????
Clidochirus_ulrichi				????? ????? ????? ????? ?????   
Hormocrinus_tenneesseensis		21100 11102 ???0? ?0010 11100
Hormocrinus_anglicus			21100 11102 ???0? ?0010 11100
Hormocrinus_quebecensis			21100 11102 ???0? ?0010 11100
Homalocrinus_nanus				20100 11122 0?0?0 00010 11112
Homalocrinus_liljevalli			20100 11122 0?0?0 00010 11112   
Kyphosocrinus_tetreaulti		11101 01100 120?? ?0010 10112
Anticosticrinus_natiscotecensis	10100 01100 120?? ?0010 10110

;

END;

	Begin mrbayes;	
	
[set up likelihood model of character evolution]
	lset applyto=(all) rates=equal coding=variable;

[set up clade constraints]
constraint node2 partial = 10-42 : 8-9; 
constraint protaxocrinus = 13-24;
constraint node3 = 10-12 25-42;
constraint node4 = 10-12 25-26 28-42; 
constraint node5 = 10-12 25 28-42; 
constraint sagenocrinida = 10-12 25 28-42;
constraint anisocrinidae = 10-12 41-42;
constraint anisocrinus = 11-12 42;
constraint node6 = 25 28-40;
constraint icthyocrinidae = 28-35;
constraint icthyocrinus = 28-29;
constraint node7 = 25 36-40;
constraint hormocrinus = 36-38;
constraint node8 = 25 39-40;
constraint homalocrinus = 39-40;


[calibrate priors on stratigraphic ranges] 

calibrate Cupulocrinus_humilis = uniform(449.1,453);
calibrate Cupulocrinus_angustatus = uniform(445.2,453);
calibrate Cupulocrinus_canaliculatus = uniform(453,458.4);
calibrate Cupulocrinus_crossmani = uniform(445.2,453);		
calibrate Cupulocrinus_heterocostalis = uniform(449.2,453);	
calibrate Cupulocrinus_jewetti = uniform(449.1,458.4);
calibrate Cupulocrinus_levorsoni = uniform(453,458.4);
calibrate Cupulocrinus_polydactylus = uniform(433.4,445.2);
calibrate Cupulocrinus_sepulchrum = uniform(443.0,445.2);	
calibrate Proanisocrinus_oswegoensis = uniform(445.2,453);	
calibrate Anisocrinus_prinstaensi = uniform(443.8,445.2);
calibrate Anisocrinus_interradiatus = uniform(423.4,433.4);
calibrate Protaxocrinus_ovalis = uniform(427.4,453);
calibrate Protaxocrinus_aberrans = uniform(427.4,428.6);
calibrate Protaxocrinus_amii = uniform(427.4,443.8);
calibrate Protaxocrinus_anellus = uniform(427.4,443.8);
calibrate Protaxocrinus_cataractensis = uniform(427.4,443.8);
calibrate Protaxocrinus_elegans	= uniform(445.2,453);
calibrate Protaxocrinus_girardeau = uniform(443.8,445.2);
calibrate Protaxocrinus_girvanensis = uniform(445.2,453.0);	
calibrate Protaxocrinus_interbrachiatus = uniform(423.4,433.4);
calibrate Protaxocrinus_laevis = uniform(449.1,453);
calibrate Protaxocrinus_paraios = uniform(443.8,445.2);
calibrate Protaxocrinus_robustus = uniform(427.4,443.8);
calibrate Tintinnabulicrinus_estoniensis = uniform(449.1,455.7);
calibrate Paerticrinus_arvosus = uniform(440.8, 443.8);
calibrate Ladacrinus_asynaptos = uniform(433.8,443.4);
calibrate Icthyocrinus_laevus = fixed(423);
calibrate Icthyocrinus_gotlandicus = uniform(423,433.4);
calibrate Clidochirus_anebos = uniform(445.2,453);	
calibrate Clidochirus_americanus = uniform(433.4,443.8);
calibrate Clidochirus_serrulatus = uniform(443.8,445.2);
calibrate Clidochirus_vaurealensis = uniform(443.8,445.2);
calibrate Clidochirus_springeri = uniform(433.4,443.8);
calibrate Clidochirus_ulrichi = uniform(433.4,443.8);
calibrate Hormocrinus_tenneesseensis = uniform(423,433.4);
calibrate Hormocrinus_anglicus = uniform(423.4,433.4);
calibrate Hormocrinus_quebecensis = uniform(427.4,428.6);
calibrate Homalocrinus_nanus = uniform(427.4,433.4);	
calibrate Homalocrinus_liljevalli = uniform(423.4,433.4);
calibrate Kyphosocrinus_tetreaulti = uniform(433.4, 438.5);
calibrate Anticosticrinus_natiscotecensis = uniform(440.8,445.2);
	
[set prior distributions on tree shape, node ages, and blens]
	prset treeagepr = offsetexp(453, 455.7); 
	prset nodeagepr = calibrated; [set node age priors]
	prset brlenspr = clock : fossilization;
	prset topologypr = constraints(node2,protaxocrinus,node3,node4,node5,anisocrinidae,anisocrinus,node6,icthyocrinidae,icthyocrinus,node7,hormocrinus,node8,homalocrinus);


[SA-FBD and relaxed morpho-clock settings] 
	prset speciationpr = uniform(0,10);
	prset extinctionpr = beta(1,1);
	prset fossilizationpr = beta(1,1);
	prset samplestrat = random;
	prset sampleprob = 1;
	prset clockvarpr = Igr;
    prset clockratepr = normal(0.0025,0.1);   [truncated normal, mean=0.08, but very flat; see Supp Table 2 of Matzke & Wright 2016]
	prset Igrvarpr = exp(1);
	

[mcmc settings]
	mcmcp ngen=20000000 samplefreq=10000 printfreq=5000 nruns=2 nchains=4 relburnin=yes burninfrac=0.25 temp = 0.1 savebrlens=yes;
	mcmc;
	sump;
	sumt;

	end;
	








[
